Well, simple answer: maybe you're right, maybe you're not - *I*
would like to have this feature.
Not so simple answer: I (umh, that's me, Ralph Kupfer, not one of
the characters I'm playing...:-)) am basically free in my
decision whether or not to act lawful. I can't decide to have
an IQ of 200, though.
So the alignment should be class-independent; special abilities,
of course, shouldn't. (And I really would like to see MUCH more
class-dependent special abilities, btw...)
I have no problem with the idea of a neutral or a chaotic knight.
Maybe Sir Galahad was the prototype for this class, but there were
traitors even at King Arthur's Court; and I bet a lot of those
so-called knights were just mercenaries...
Same for the other classes.
And no, I don't think that henceforth everyone would play only
neutral characters...I wouldn't...:-)
But if this change is considered to be unbalancing - add a few
other changes:
- No wishing for non-coaligned weapons. Think about the challenge
  playing a chaotic valkyrie with no mojo-jojo; a neutral knight
  without Excalibur but Mjollnir, which he can't wield because
  he's not strong enough...:-)
- Even make it more or less impossible to use non-coal. weapons -
  10% HP-drain per round or something.
- Make helms of opposite align. MUCH less common.
And, because it would be the players decision: if you think an elf
has to be chaotic - choose "c" when asked for your alignment.
Long ago, in the dark ages, even in Nethack elves were lawful...
so things do change, don't they? 
So let us add this change...

Comments?

Ralph



